1
00:03:32,500 --> 00:03:38,500
Last Kind Words is a romance, drama, mystery film directed by Kevin Barker.

2
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:11,000
17-year old Eli moves with his family to the isolated farm of reclusive
Waylon, a man whose dark past threatens to overtake him.

3
00:10:37,500 --> 00:10:43,500
Eli’s family works to restore the desolate fields, while
he becomes fascinated with the forests.

4
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:16,000
While on the farm, Eli meets the mysterious Amanda when she gives him an apple.

5
00:17:42,500 --> 00:17:48,500
The next day she extracts a promise from him to avoid the deep woods.

6
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:21,000
Reeling from a violent encounter with his father, one night he breaks
this promise and finds her body hanging from a tree.

7
00:24:47,500 --> 00:24:53,500
Waylon, played by Brad Dourif.

8
00:28:20,000 --> 00:28:26,000
Eli, played by Spencer Daniels.

9
00:31:52,500 --> 00:31:58,500
Amanda, played by Alexia Fast.

10
00:35:25,000 --> 00:35:31,000
Ida, played by Marianne Hagan.

11
00:38:57,500 --> 00:39:03,500
Katie, played by Sarah Steele.

12
00:42:30,000 --> 00:42:36,000
Bud, played by Clay Wilcox.

13
00:46:02,500 --> 00:46:08,500
A person's last words, their final articulated words stated prior to death or as death approaches, are often
recorded because of the decedent's fame, but sometimes because of interest in the statement itself.

14
00:49:35,000 --> 00:49:41,000
(People dying of illness are frequently inarticulate at the end, and in such cases their actual last utterances may not be
recorded or considered very important.) Last words may be recorded accurately, or, for a variety of reasons, may not.

15
00:53:07,500 --> 00:53:13,500
Reasons can include simple error or deliberate intent.

16
00:56:40,000 --> 00:56:46,000
Even if reported wrongly, putative last words can constitute an important part of the perceived
historical records or demonstration of cultural attitudes toward death at the time.

17
01:00:12,500 --> 01:00:18,500
Charles Darwin, for example, was reported to have disavowed his theory of
evolution in favor of traditional religious faith at his death.

18
01:03:45,000 --> 01:03:51,000
This widely disseminated report served the interests of those
who opposed Darwin's theory on religious grounds.

19
01:07:17,500 --> 01:07:23,500
However, the putative witness had not been at Darwin's deathbed
or seen him at any time near the end of his life.

20
01:10:50,000 --> 01:10:56,000
Cultural traditions around the world ascribe special significance to words uttered at or near
death, but the form and content of reported last words may depend on cultural context.

21
01:14:22,500 --> 01:14:28,500
There is a tradition in Hindu and Buddhist cultures of an expectation of a meaningful farewell statement; Zen
monks by long custom are expected to compose a poem on the spot and recite it with their last breath.

22
01:17:55,000 --> 01:18:01,000
In Western culture particular attention has been paid to last words which demonstrate
deathbed salvation – the repentance of sins and affirmation of faith.

23
01:21:27,500 --> 01:21:33,500
The tone is dark and emotional and mind_bending.
